- Summary:: Critics raise concerns about AI-driven personalized education in higher education, emphasizing the importance of human-to-human tutoring for impactful learning experiences. AI's potential for customization in education may risk isolating students, limiting exposure to diverse perspectives and hindering the development of critical thinking skills. The balance between AI-driven personalization and maintaining the social, diverse, and challenging aspects of education is crucial for preparing students to navigate a complex world.
